# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 serving window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of serving/tp4-s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled
# in by whoever drives the window; every other value is final. ORDER.txt says the order, each job's image and its stop rule.
# EV-R0: an all-four reset with the heal, and nothing else, straight before the one-card evidence jobs. The four-card gate jobs leave
# the ring fabric on the ethernet cores, and card M alone then fails to open ("Read 0xffffffff over PCIe ...: the board should be
# reset"): the first CB1 candidate (v140) lost a run this way and passed after an all-four reset. A pair-only reset would leave M's
# links to the other boards untrained on this cabling, so it is the four-card reset; the profile only satisfies the job parser
# (nothing is served). Duration (estimate): reset 3-12 min, heal up to 3 more. Stop rule: a reset or heal failure stops the window.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-stackfix-3
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
